--TEST--
Writing an element of a `readonly` array property writes the property, so after the first write it is a second one (`rule:classes/lateinit-restrictions`)
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The constructor sets `$items`, then changes one element and adds another.
// Each element write stores a new array in `$items`, so both are second writes.
class Bag {
    public readonly array<int> $items;

    public function constructor() {
        $this->items = [1];
        $this->items[0] = 5;
        $this->items[] = 6;
    }
}

var $g = new Bag();
// covers: lang:classes/properties
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0782]: `Bag::$items` is `readonly`, so the constructor writes it only once
%A
error[E0782]: `Bag::$items` is `readonly`, so the constructor writes it only once
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
